      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Proponents argue that school vouchers empower parents by allowing them to choose the best educational fit for their children, especially when public schools fail them. They see it as a necessary market correction that increases competition and improves overall educational quality. Opponents, however, argue that vouchers drain vital public funding from already struggling public schools, effectively diverting taxpayer money away from the system meant to serve the most vulnerable students. This is a fundamental debate over whether education is a right provided by the state or a service that can be purchased.",
